        <mxCell id="p13c87" value="&lt;b&gt;Independent of both&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=2;spacingBottom=2;fontSize=11;arcSize=8;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=10.5;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1230" y="972" width="330" height="40" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p13c88" value="&lt;b&gt;What this means for replacing Provideam&lt;/b&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontSize=14;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1038" width="1500" height="24" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p13c89" value="1. Overlap rows: Insights Hub can supply the data, but the numbers differ. On the overlap days the Insights Hub good parts are 96.6% (B2) and 43.6% (GT4) of the Provideam good parts. Reckitt must name the official source per site.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;2. Only Provideam: we need the Provideam files or the Provideam rules. Or Reckitt accepts that the column is empty (for example comment text).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;3. Excel files: they do not depend on the OEE source. We need them in every case.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;4. At a switch, the history in the report changes: Provideam numbers before the date, Insights Hub numbers after it." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=2;spacingBottom=2;fontSize=11;arcSize=8;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#666666;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=8;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1072" width="1520" height="150" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram><diagram name="Background: Data collection and conflicts" id="page14">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1400" dy="900" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="0" pageScale="1" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" /><mxCell id="bg-note" value="&lt;b&gt;Background page (state of 2026-10-14, copied from powerbi-data-map.drawio)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Since then: the files are copied by hand to the lake (eu_report/reference, eu_report/pbi_report/source); the listener rebuilds the tables when a file changes." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;fontSize=11;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="-60" width="1000" height="50" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p14c2" value="&lt;b&gt;Data collection: how each data item reaches the lake and where it conflicts with Insights Hub&lt;/b&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontSize=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="20" width="1500" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p14c3" value="Status 2026-10-14, from the downloaded SharePoint files (Hull, Nottingham, Weinheim; Mira and most Hull folders not reachable). Collection today: the user copies files by hand to the data lake. Next step: Power Automate sends the file to a VFC endpoint, the VFC writes a parquet file. Not tested: file size limit, key handling and POST on the VFC http in node." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=2;spacingBottom=2;fontSize=11;arcSize=8;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#666666;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="62" width="1520" height="62" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p14c4" value="&lt;b&gt;Files (Provideam reports and Excel files kept by hand)&lt;/b&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="146" width="700" height="20" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p14c5" value="SharePoint folder (Hull and Nottingham sites)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=2;spacingBottom=2;fontSize=11;arcSize=8;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#666666;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=10.5;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="170" width="235" height="62" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p14c6" value="NOW: the user copies the file by hand" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=2;spacingBottom=2;fontSize=11;arcSize=8;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=10.5;" vertex="1" parent="1">
